# Build-context allowlist discipline for a `COPY . .` Dockerfile.
#
# This image is built in GitHub Actions and pushed to a container registry, so
# anything the build context includes can end up in a published layer. Keep
# this file a STRICT SUPERSET of .gitignore's secret patterns: .gitignore uses
# the glob `.env*`, and this file used to exclude only the literal `.env.local`
# — every other env-file name would have been copied straight into the image.

# --- secrets & local config (patterns, never literals) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.local.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
**/credentials*.json
**/service-account*.json

# --- VCS, CI, agent scaffolding — none of it belongs in a runtime image ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
deploy

# --- build outputs & caches (rebuilt inside the image) ---
node_modules
.next
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.DS_Store

# --- dev-only assets (15MB of screenshots, playwright scripts) ---
screenshots
scripts
